`openhd_pi_vid` accepts an Annex-B H.264 elementary stream from a file or
stdin.  This is compatible with the OpenHD X21/RV1126(B) MPP encoder output
after RTP depacketization:

    openhd_pi_vid stream.h264
    cat stream.h264 | openhd_pi_vid -

`fpv_video0.bin` is a compatibility name for the same player.

On Pi 4 and CM4 with FKMS, use `--hevc` for an 8-bit Annex-B H.265 stream:

    openhd_pi_vid --hevc stream.h265
    cat stream.h265 | openhd_pi_vid --hevc -

H.265 uses the Pi's V4L2 hardware decoder through FFmpeg and presents its
SAND128 DMA buffers through the firmware video renderer at layer -128.

The old X20 recovery-header probe is opt-in with `--x20`; normal X21/RV1126(B)
streams should be run without it. `--eof` is available for sources that need
explicit OMX end-of-frame flags.
